translate en b45_001:
    "Kai walks out of the station concourse. His steps feel light — lighter than any step he's taken all year. This afternoon's storm has passed. The asphalt is still wet, streetlights are flickering on one by one, and his chest feels… open. That hollow ache that sat heavy in him for months has finally melted away."

translate en b45_002:
    kai_hati "Yara didn't leave me. She just moved to another city. \"Goodbye\" is… a pause. Just a pause. How did something that simple take me a whole year to figure out?"

translate en b45_003:
    "His feet move on their own. Without thinking, without deciding — the sidewalk pulls him down a turn he knows by heart. The dead-end alley. Gema Masa."

translate en b45_004:
    "The bell above the door chimes softly. It's quiet inside — not the eerie, suffocating quiet from before. Pak Ageng sits in his rocking chair behind the teak counter. He's much thinner than he was a few weeks ago. The lines on his face run deeper. His eyes are a little cloudy, like he's looking at something far beyond this room."

translate en b45_005:
    kai_hati "Pak Ageng looks… so tired. When did he get this thin?"

translate en b45_006:
    ageng "{i}(turns slowly, smiling — the most genuine smile Kai has ever seen on him){/i} You came back, son. And you brought your soul home with you."

translate en b45_007:
    kai "{i}(walks up to the counter, nodding slowly){/i} You were right, Pak. Goodbye's just a pause. I don't have to be scared of what's ahead anymore."

translate en b45_008:
    ageng "{i}(chuckles softly, holding back a small cough){/i} Good. Good… {i}(reaches very slowly into a drawer under the counter, pulling out a Type IV Metal cassette still sealed in plastic){/i} This is for you, Kai. The last tape from this shop. On the house."

translate en b45_009:
    "He sets the tape on the counter. No red label. No handwritten date. The white paper label is completely blank."

translate en b45_010:
    kai "{i}(stares at the cassette){/i} What tape is this, Pak? Why's the label blank?"

translate en b45_011:
    ageng "This is the tape of your real future. Everything you'd ever want to hear after today is on there. {i}(looks at Kai with the warmth of a teacher letting a student go){/i} Play it, if you want to know which path to take."

translate en b45_012:
    "Kai stares at the blank cassette for a long moment. The clear casing catches the glow of the hanging lamp. In the back of his mind, that old temptation whispers faintly — imagining everything he could hear from the rest of his life with Yara. But only for a second."

translate en b45_013:
    kai "{i}(smiles faintly, shaking his head; picks up the tape and slips it into his jacket pocket — seal unbroken){/i} Thank you, Pak. But I'm not going to play it. I want the tape to stay blank… until I fill it myself. With real sounds."

translate en b45_014:
    ageng "{i}(freezes for a beat — then laughs warmly, the most relieved laugh Kai has ever heard from the old man){/i} A very wise choice, Kai. You're finally, truly free."

translate en b45_015:
    "That night in his room, Kai opens his desk drawer. Inside sits a tangle of tape pulled from old cassettes — none of them holding any power over him anymore. He pushes them aside and picks up the last tape from Pak Ageng."

translate en b45_016a:
    kai_hati "My hand reaches for the Walkman… then stops. {i}(smiles quietly to himself){/i} No. Not because I'm scared. Precisely because I'm not scared anymore. I'll play this tape — later, when I actually have something worth listening to. And that day will come."

translate en b45_017a:
    "Kai sets the cassette in the corner of the drawer, blank label facing up. Like a promise left right where he can see it."

translate en b45_016b:
    kai_hati "Not yet. Let the tape stay blank for now. I'll live my life first — the tape can wait."

translate en b45_017b:
    "Kai tucks that last tape from Pak Ageng into the deepest corner of the drawer and shuts it tight. Some things really are meant for later."

translate en b46t_001:
    "A few months later. Dry-season winds sweep through Malang, crisp but still carrying a late-afternoon chill. Kai walks along with a college backpack slung over one shoulder — his thick gray jacket swapped out for a casual flannel shirt."

translate en b46t_001_p2:
    "His stride is steady. Architecture school eats up his time — scale models, drafting assignments, late nights — yet in between it all, he can always breathe."

translate en b46t_002:
    kai_hati "And somehow… my feet turned down here again. Old habits die hard, huh."

translate en b46t_003:
    "The alley is clean now, its brick walls glowing gold in the sunset. At the far end, though, Kai slows down. The wooden door of Gema Masa no longer hangs with a rusty padlock chain. The little \"Open/Closed\" sign is gone. Taped to the freshly spotless front window is a large sheet of white paper in bold print:"

translate en b46t_004:
    "FOR RENT."

translate en b46t_005:
    "Kai steps onto the porch and peers inside. Completely empty. No glass cabinets packed with hundreds of fates. No teak counter where Pak Ageng used to brew coffee and serve cenil. Even the old rocking chair is gone. Just clean wooden floors and long evening shadows."

translate en b46t_006:
    kai_hati "Pak Ageng is gone. The shop too. The little shop born out of grief… its work is done. {i}(brushes his hand gently across the windowpane){/i} Thank you, Pak. Never got to say it in person. So this'll have to do."

translate en b46t_007:
    "The phone in his pocket buzzes. Incoming video call — contact name: Yara. Kai pops in an earphone and taps accept. Yara's bright face fills the screen; she's sitting in a cozy cafe in Yogyakarta, her big black headphones draped around her neck as usual."

translate en b46t_008:
    yara "Hey, Kai!"

translate en b46t_009:
    kai "Hey, Yara. Just got out of class?"

translate en b46t_010:
    yara "Yeah, just now. Today I learned how to filter low-end frequencies in the studio. {i}(holds her phone closer to the cafe window){/i} Hey, listen to this, Kai."

translate en b46t_011:
    yara "Beautiful, right?"

translate en b46t_012:
    kai "{i}(smiles, looking at his reflection in the empty shop window right beside Yara's face on his screen){/i} So beautiful."

translate en b46t_013:
    kai_hati "Hundreds of kilometers away. Yet her voice feels right here. Turns out distance isn't a wall. Just… a bridge that sounds a little different. — I might never remember how we first met in the library."

translate en b46t_013_p2:
    kai_hati "That hole is still there. A scar from my crazy past. And that's okay. We're writing a new story now. Today, tomorrow, and every day after that. No predictions."

translate en b46t_014:
    kai "I miss you, Yara."

translate en b46t_015:
    yara "Miss you too, Kai. See you at the station at the end of the month, okay?"

translate en b46t_016:
    kai "{i}(nods firmly){/i} Yeah. At the station."

translate en b46t_017:
    "Kai turns and walks out of the alley toward the bustling main street. Safe in his jacket pocket sits the blank tape Pak Ageng gave him — quiet proof that his future is his own now, to write and listen to, surprises and all."

translate en b46s_001:
    "A few months later, Kai's feet bring him back down that alley. Gema Masa is empty now — a \"FOR RENT\" sign taped to its clean window. Pak Ageng is gone, and the shop's work is done. Kai smiles faintly at the empty glass, then reaches into his jacket pocket."

translate en b46s_002:
    kai_hati "Not a blank tape. And not a prediction. We recorded everything on here ourselves — the boiling pot in the cafeteria, train tracks, rain on the shop porch… and all our ugly laughs. This tape is full. Full because we filled it, not because someone handed it to us."

translate en b46s_003:
    "His phone buzzes. A video call from Yara, from her little cafe in Yogyakarta."

translate en b46s_004:
    yara "Hey, Kai! Where are you? Wait, that background looks like… {i}(squints){/i} Is that the alley to Pak Ageng's shop?"

translate en b46s_005:
    kai "Yeah. Just stopping by the empty shop. {i}(holds up their cassette to the camera){/i} Look. I still carry it around. Played it back at my boarding room yesterday — the part where you're laughing in the rain is still the loudest thing on there."

translate en b46s_006:
    yara "{i}(laughs){/i} That wasn't laughing, I was freezing! Oh, wait — I'm coming home to Malang at the end of the month. Let's record Side B, okay? At the station. It's gotta be the station."

translate en b46s_007:
    kai "Deal. Side B at the station."

translate en b46s_008:
    kai_hati "There aren't any holes in my memory — because I never traded a thing away. All there is, is a tape getting fuller and fuller. And everything on it… we're writing ourselves."

translate en b46s_009:
    "Kai steps out of the alley onto the lively main street, the cassette tucked safe in his pocket — not to sneak a peek at tomorrow, but to replay whenever he wants to remember today."

translate en b47_001:
    "Two years pass. The dead-end alley isn't silent anymore: cool post-rain air, a warm hum of chatter, and at the very end — Gema Masa has been transformed. The heavy wooden door has been replaced by a black iron-framed glass door."

translate en b47_001_p2:
    "Inside, a long coffee bar with a gleaming espresso machine stands where the cassette cabinets used to line the wall. Pak Ageng's rocking chair has given way to cushioned wooden seats and a long table cluttered with laptops, tracing paper, and ceramic mugs."

translate en b47_002:
    teman1 "Kai! Over here, rek — pull up a chair, the site model's almost done!"

translate en b47_003:
    "At the corner table — the exact spot where the red-tape cabinet used to stand — two of Kai's architecture classmates are buried in tracing paper, cardboard cutouts, and a laptop showing a 3D model."

translate en b47_004:
    kai "{i}(drops his heavy backpack and sits down){/i} Sorry I'm a bit late. Had a structures review first. {i}(grabs the iced americano they already ordered for him and takes a sip){/i} Ah. Back among the living."

translate en b47_005:
    teman2 "{i}(without taking his eyes off the screen){/i} No worries. We just need to clean up the terrain contours behind the building. Seriously though, Kai, this spot you recommended is top-tier. Quiet, the coffee's good tenan, and somehow… the vibe just makes you focus."

translate en b47_006:
    kai "{i}(smiles faintly, letting his eyes wander around the room){/i} Yeah. This place really is… something else."

translate en b47_007:
    kai_hati "To them, it's just a great coffee shop to get studio work done. To me… behind these exposed walls, sometimes I still swear I can hear a cassette turning softly. The hiss of tape. Pak Ageng's laugh as he served cenil. The old echoes are gone — replaced by living ones. And that's okay. Better, even."

translate en b47_008:
    "Kai remembers the first time he pushed open that glass door, not long after the shop opened. Back then he stood in front of the bar for ages, reading the menu board — in the exact spot where the teak counter used to be."

translate en b47_009a:
    barista "One black coffee. For here?"

translate en b47_010a:
    kai "For here. {i}(sits facing the bar){/i} Staying here… a while."

translate en b47_009b:
    barista "One hot tea. For here?"

translate en b47_010b:
    kai "For here. {i}(smiles quietly to himself — the jasmine tea in this shop used to always be free; now he pays for it, and it still tastes just as warm){/i}"

translate en b47_009c:
    kai "Not ordering just yet, Mas. Mind if I just sit for a bit?"

translate en b47_010c:
    barista "Sure, make yourself at home."

translate en b47_011c:
    kai_hati "Back then I just needed to sit. Make sure this place had truly become somewhere new — and that I was okay with it."

translate en b47_012:
    "While his friends dive back into debating columns and rooflines, Kai's phone buzzes. A message from Yara — with a ten-second voice note attached."

translate en b47_013:
    yara_pesan "\"Kai, listen to this! I just recorded rain falling on the tin roof of Stasiun Tugu this afternoon. It sounds just like the echo at Stasiun Malang Kota Lama two years ago. I miss you.\""

translate en b47_014:
    "Kai puts in one earphone and hits play. Yogyakarta rain fills his ear, blending right into the hiss of the espresso machine and his friends' chatter. He closes his eyes for a moment."

translate en b47_015:
    kai_hati "Right here in this exact spot, I used to tremble thinking about tomorrow. Now I'm sitting here celebrating today. Learning. Laughing with friends. And loving Yara — with a melody we write ourselves, every single day. No more fortune-telling tapes."

translate en b47_016a:
    "His first black coffee here is long gone. All that lingers is the taste — bitter, honest, with nothing left to predict."

translate en b47_016b:
    "The tea he ordered that afternoon went cold. That's okay. In this place, even cold tea was once the start of everything."

translate en b47_016c:
    "Sometimes all you really need is to sit. In the same chair, in the same corner — as someone new."

translate en b48_001:
    "Four years. Countless all-nighters, crumpled tracing paper, and endless model revisions — all folded neatly into one architecture degree. Kai defended his thesis last week."

translate en b48_001_p2:
    "This afternoon his room is messy in the most relieving way: cardboard boxes packed with structural textbooks, drafting triangles, and old drafts. College is over. A new chapter, as a young architect, is about to begin."

translate en b48_002:
    "While clearing out the deepest drawer of his desk — one he hasn't touched in years — Kai's fingers bump against something hard in the very back corner. A clear plastic shell."

translate en b48_003:
    kai_hati "This is… {i}(pulls it out, blowing a thin layer of dust off the surface){/i} The last tape from Pak Ageng. Seal still unbroken. Label still blank. Four years, and I never dared— no, it's not that I didn't dare."

translate en b48_003_p2:
    kai_hati "I just never needed to. {i}(pauses; eyes drifting to the old silver Walkman on his bookshelf){/i} I used to be scared out of my mind of this tape. Now all that's left is… missing the man who gave it to me."

translate en b48_004:
    kai "{i}(sits on the edge of the bed, slowly peeling off the plastic wrap){/i} Pak… I'm gonna play it now, okay?"

translate en b48_005:
    "A soft hiss flows through. Then three seconds of silence. Kai holds his breath. And the voice that comes out makes his eyes go wide."

translate en b48_006:
    yara_kaset "—hey, put the candles in the middle! Kai, hurry up and cut the cake, I'm starving!"

translate en b48_007:
    kai_kaset "Hold on, Yar, the lighter's jammed. There — come on, blow them out together! One… two… three!"

translate en b48_008:
    "That's Yara's voice — bright, grown-up, laughing without a care in the world. And the second voice is Kai's own: a genuinely happy twenty-two-year-old, right in the middle of his simple birthday celebration at his rented place just a few months ago. Kai sinks back onto the bed. Tears spill down his face before he even realizes it."

translate en b48_009:
    kai_hati "How is that even possible… This tape was sealed four years ago. My birthday was only a few months back. How could it have recorded that? {i}(a long pause; then the realization slowly sinks in){/i} …Oh. Oh, Pak. This tape never recorded fate. Nothing in that shop ever recorded fate."

translate en b48_009_p2:
    kai_hati "What it recorded was… potential happiness. The resonance of every good choice I've made since that day at the station. Every time I chose to trust today instead of fearing tomorrow — this tape tuned itself to it. Recording the echo of the happiness that was meant to be mine."

translate en b48_010:
    "Kai slips off his earphones slowly. He looks down at the tape in his hand, smiling through his tears. Warmth spreads all through his chest. His goodbye to Pak Ageng really is forever — yet the echo of the old man's wisdom will stay tucked safely inside him."

translate en b48_011:
    kai_hati "Goodbye to you too, Pak. And… thank you. For everything."

translate en b48_012:
    "Kai walks over to the window, pulls the curtains open, and lets Malang's late-afternoon sun wash over his face. Out there, a noisy, beautiful world is waiting — and this time, he's ready to live every single second of it. To his own melody."

translate en ep_h2_001:
    "That night in his room, Kai tidies up his desk and finds a small cassette he and Yara recorded together — not a prophecy tape, not a bargain. Just an ordinary tape holding a moment too bright to let slip away."

translate en ep_h2_002:
    kai "{i}(smiling softly, slipping the cassette into the old silver Walkman on his desk){/i} Let's give it a quick spin."

translate en ep_h2_003:
    "Their laughter fills the warm room. There's no prophecy on this tape — only real voices they made themselves. Kai takes off his earphones, smiles calmly, and steps toward tomorrow without fear."
